/-!
# STR029.21: Equivariance of the unique range graph

Task id: STR029.21 (node STR029, frontier unit, leaf formalization).
Title: Equivariance of the unique range graph.

Statement. Let `T_θ u (t) = u (t - θ)`. The smooth graph `ψ` of STR029.16 (the unique solution of
the variational range equation `R (a, b, h, γ, w) = 0`) is equivariant under `T_{2π/3}` and under
the reflection `t ↦ -t`, with the induced rotation and reflection of `(a, b)`. It also satisfies
`ψ (-a, -b, -h, γ) = T_π ψ (a, b, h, γ)`. On the symmetry invariant neighborhoods of STR029.16 the
functions `F (a, b, h, γ) = J (h, γ, a cos t + b sin t + ψ (a, b, h, γ))` and
`V (h, A, B, s) = F (h A, h B, h, h² s) / h⁴` have the corresponding rotation and reflection
invariances, and `V (-h, A, B, s) = V (h, A, B, s)`.

## Provides

* `DGPS.Frontier.STR029.str029_21_equivariance_unique_range_graph`: the main statement. There are
  `U`, `V`, `ψ` as in STR029.16 (all of its conjuncts are repeated) such that, for `p ∈ U`,
  `ψ` commutes with the rotation by `2π k / 3` (`T_{2π k/3}`), the reflection and the sign map
  (`T_π`) in the pointwise form, the function `F` is invariant under the three induced parameter
  maps, and `V` is invariant under the rotation of `(A, B)` by `2π k / 3`, under `B ↦ -B` and
  under `h ↦ -h`, at all points whose `(h A, h B, h, h² s)` lies in `U`.

Supporting declarations (all carry the suffix `_STR02921`):

* `SymOK_STR02921 σ c ε`: the circle isometry `t ↦ σ t + c`, `σ = ±1`, maps `cos 3t` to
  `ε cos 3t` and `sin 3t` to `σ ε sin 3t`; `symOK_rot_STR02921`, `symOK_refl_STR02921` and
  `symOK_half_STR02921` are the instances for `T_{2π k/3}`, the reflection and `T_π`.
* `actPar_STR02921 σ c ε`: the induced action on the parameters `(a, b, h, γ)`;
  `actPar_rot_STR02921`, `actPar_refl_STR02921` and `actPar_sign_STR02921` identify it with
  `rotPar_STR02916`, `reflPar_STR02916` and `signPar_STR02916`.
* `rho_pb_STR02921`, `gradG12_pb_STR02921`, `gradG_pb_STR02921`, `projP_pb_STR02921`,
  `uT_pb_STR02921`: the pullback of the density, of the gradient `G`, of the projection `P` and
  of the chart function along the isometry.
* `Rval_STR02921`, `Rval_act_STR02921`, `Rzero_iff_STR02921`: the pointwise values of the
  variational range map `R` and its naturality, `R (g p, g w) = 0 ↔ R (p, w) = 0`.
* `GraphData_STR02921 U V ψ`: the properties of the STR029.16 graph that are used.
* `graph_act_STR02921`: the equivariance `ψ (g p) = g ψ (p)` of any graph with the uniqueness
  property of STR029.16 on isometry invariant sets; `graph_rot_STR02921`, `graph_refl_STR02921`,
  `graph_sign_STR02921` are its three generators in `E`, and `psi_rot_STR02921`,
  `psi_refl_STR02921`, `psi_sign_STR02921` their pointwise forms.
* `fisher_pb_STR02921`, `entropy_pb_STR02921`, `Jchart_pb_STR02921`: invariance of the chart
  functional `J` under the isometry.
* `Fgraph_STR02921`, `Vgraph_STR02921`: the functions `F` and `V` built from a graph `ψ`;
  `F_act_STR02921`, `F_rot_STR02921`, `F_refl_STR02921`, `F_sign_STR02921` are the invariances of
  `F`, and `V_rot_STR02921`, `V_refl_STR02921`, `V_sign_STR02921` those of `V`.

## R5 notes

* No hypothesis is added to the statement. It is one existence claim for `(U, V, ψ)`, obtained from
  `str029_16_unique_smooth_range_graph`, carrying all conjuncts of STR029.16 together with the
  equivariances. Nothing is asserted outside `U`: no unrestricted global graph appears, and every
  evaluation of `ψ`, `F`, `V` is at a point of `U` whose images under the symmetries lie in `U` by
  the invariance of `U` supplied by STR029.16.
* The range map is the variational range map `Rpar_STR02916` of STR029.15 and STR029.16 (the
  projection `P` of the gradient `G` of STR029.50 in the chart `u = a cos t + b sin t + w`). It is
  not the Euler range map, and no identification of the two is used. The explicit formula of
  STR029.12 enters through `gradG_STR02912` (equal to `gradG_STR02950` by `gradG_eq_STR02912`), and
  the reference symmetries of STR029.04 enter through the periodicity of `cos 3t`.
* `T_θ u (t) = u (t - θ)` is the pullback `pullE_STR02916 1 _ (-θ)` and the reflection is
  `pullE_STR02916 (-1) _ 0`. The equivariances are stated pointwise on the values of `ψ`:
  `ψ (rotPar θ p) (t) = ψ p (t - θ)`, `ψ (reflPar p) (t) = ψ p (-t)` and
  `ψ (signPar p) (t) = ψ p (t - π)`. The form `ψ (g p) = g (ψ p)` as an equality in `E` is
  given by the helpers `graph_rot_STR02921`, `graph_refl_STR02921` and `graph_sign_STR02921`
  (from the general `graph_act_STR02921`); the pointwise form is the evaluation of these.
* The rotation is stated for `θ = 2π k / 3` with `k` an integer (the cyclic group generated by
  `T_{2π/3}`), because the reference density `q_h` and the gradient are invariant only under these
  shifts. A general angle is not an invariance of `G`, and none is claimed. The reflection is
  `t ↦ -t`. The statement for `T_π` is paired with `h ↦ -h` since `cos 3 (t - π) = - cos 3t`.
  The remaining elements of the finite group follow by composing the generators.
* The induced action on `(a, b)`: `T_θ (a cos t + b sin t) = (a cos θ - b sin θ) cos t +
  (a sin θ + b cos θ) sin t`, which is `rotPar_STR02916 θ`; the reflection sends `(a, b)` to
  `(a, -b)`; `T_π` sends `(a, b)` to `(-a, -b)`. These are the actions defined in STR029.16.
* `F p` is `Jchart_STR02950 h γ (uT a b ψ(p))`, that is `J (h, γ, a cos t + b sin t + ψ (p))` with
  `J` the logarithmic chart functional `fisherChart - 2 (1 + γ) entropyChart` of STR029.49 and
  STR029.50, and `ψ` the total function of STR029.16. Only the values of `ψ` on `U` are meaningful.
* `V h A B s` is `F (h A, h B, h, h² s) / h⁴` for `h ≠ 0`. The invariance lemmas are stated for
  every `h` (division by zero is `0` in Lean, so the case `h = 0` is trivially consistent), and
  with the hypothesis `(h A, h B, h, h² s) ∈ U`, which is the domain of the node statement. The
  images under the symmetries lie in `U` by STR029.16. The evenness `V (-h, A, B, s) = V (h, A, B, s)`
  uses `F` invariance under the sign map and `(-h)^4 = h^4`.
* "Circle isometries preserve Haar measure, differentiation up to the reflection sign and the first
  harmonic complement" is formalized as: `meanT_pb_STR02916` (Haar measure), `deriv_pb_STR02916`
  and `deriv2_pb_STR02916` (differentiation), and `projP_pb_STR02921` (the projection `P` onto the
  complement of `1`, `cos`, `sin`). Periodicity and continuity of `G` needed for the last come from
  the Hölder carrier `Gfun_STR02955` of STR029.55.
* The carriers are those of STR029.68 and STR029.69, the log-chart densities of STR029.01, and the
  gradient of STR029.50 through STR029.55, exactly as in STR029.15 and STR029.16. No
  angular-to-physical conversion enters this unit.
-/

